What is Artificial Intelligence (AI)?
Definition: Artificial Intelligence (AI) is a field of computer science that enables machines to perform tasks that normally require human intelligence.
Purpose: AI helps machines mimic human thinking and decision-making.
Unlike Traditional Programming: Instead of following only predefined rules, AI systems learn patterns from data to make predictions and decisions.
Capabilities of AI:
Learning from data
Reasoning and problem-solving
Decision-making
Understanding and generating human language
Recognizing images, speech, and faces
Real-World Examples:
ChatGPT
Google Maps (route optimization)
Gmail Spam Filter
Netflix/YouTube Recommendation Systems
Face Recognition (phone unlock, security systems)
Interview Answer (Short)

Q: What is Artificial Intelligence?

A: Artificial Intelligence (AI) is a branch of computer science that enables machines to perform tasks that usually require human intelligence, such as learning, reasoning, decision-making, and understanding language. 
Unlike traditional programming, AI learns patterns from data instead of relying only on predefined rules. Common examples include ChatGPT, Google Maps, Gmail spam filtering, recommendation systems, and face recognition.
